{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1540363-non-exp-based-awards","id":1540363,"title":"Non-Exp based Awards","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-08-14T09:31:52-07:00","id":1540363,"title":"Non-Exp based Awards","content":"Really I'm starting this because I'm looking for an old thread that I think HeavyArms or Anubis or Telgar commented on which was an in depth explanation of why they never award Werewolf players with Gifts or Charms. <br /> <br /> I find it interesting that backgrounds are supposed to be almost entirely the purview of the ST to award or deduct based on story beats, and Rites and Rituals are supposed to be learned in in-character scenes, Merits are supposed to be fairly static, and Flaws are similarly static but have rules for being bought off or being applied by catastrophic events. <br /> <br /> I know a house rule that a lot of tables I've played at has been borrowed from Call of Cthulhu has been to say that you can only spend exp. to raise stats that you've used in the last story arc, although my own group has become more flexible with that by including 'bluebooked' downtime scenes as validation for raising stats.<br /> <br /> It feels to me like you should be able to award a gift purely as a sign of favor from some spirit, like they've imprinted a little bit of themselves on your garou and changed how their shifter mantle manifests. Like obviously all of these are subject to Rule0 wherein if the ST thinks it'd be cool for the story and the table agrees, do whatever, but I assume that there are logical or narrative or balance reasons why some things are meant to be awarded and some things are meant to be purchased for points. But I think there should be more character resources characters can buy for points.","signature":"","edited":{"use